    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d835">

                <pb facs="0759" n="752" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg752"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/11364: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-03T16:00:00-05:00">December 3, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>327. Your 580, November 30, 5 p.m. The Department desires to be informed of any
                    information available since the dispatch of your telegram under reference and of
                    your present estimate in regard to this matter.<anchor n="73" xml:id="d835-f1"
                    /></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d835-f1" n="73" xml:id="d835-f1-content">
                <p>The Secretary of State in telegram No. 4, December 3, 7 p.m., informed President
                    Roosevelt, then at sea: “We have heard nothing further on the question of a
                    declaration of war by Japan.” Then followed a brief summary of German moves.
                    (793.94/11432)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
